docs: catch the pages up with what the plugin now does

Several claims had drifted from the plugin, in both directions.

Two were promises we did not keep: the inspections and Nette pages said
a destination in `n:href` was checked, which only became true this week,
and three pages said HTML inspections work natively while thirteen of
them were switched off across every `.latte` file. Both now hold.

The asset section was the other way round: it described a state we have
moved past. `n:asset` is checked, the optional forms are recognised, and
a reference behind a mapper prefix is no longer reported at a guess. The
table and the prose say what is still missing instead: navigation, a
path that lands on a directory, a configurable root, and reading the
`assets:` section of a NEON file. The summary now says Latte Pro is
ahead in most respects rather than almost every one.

Also documented: printing a value that cannot become a string, a static
member reached through an arrow, and the refusal of a hand-written
`|escape`, the last one with the version condition that governs it.
